      "id": "summary",
      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>The Guardian’s chief culture writer Charlotte Higgins on why she was inspired to learn Ukrainian and what it taught her about its people</p><p>For <strong>Charlotte Higgins,</strong> the Guardian’s chief culture writer, visiting Ukraine and meeting the artists, novelists and poets under fire changed her life. “It was even before I went home that I decided I needed to learn some Ukrainian,” she tells <strong>Helen Pidd</strong>.</p><p>Back in London, she began having weekly lessons with <strong>Olha Makar</strong>, who was living in the far west of Ukraine and squeezed in teaching between helping displaced teenagers.</p><p><a href=\"https://guardianbookshop.com/ukrainian-lessons-9781787335974/\"><em>Ukrainian Lessons: Art in a Time of War by Charlotte Higgins</em></a><em>, is published by Jonathan Cape. To support the Guardian, order your copy at </em><a href=\"https://guardianbookshop.com/ukrainian-lessons-9781787335974/\"><em>guardianbookshop.com</em></a></p><p><em>On Wednesday 30 September, </em><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/guardian-live-events/2026/feb/24/ukrainian-lessons-art-in-a-time-of-war-with-charlotte-higgins-and-guests\"><em>join Charlotte Higgins</em></a><em> and our panel of acclaimed Ukrainian writers to reflect on the profound connections between war, art and life. With Olia Hercules, Sasha Dovzhyk and Olesya Khromeychuk. Book tickets </em><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/guardian-live-events/2026/feb/24/ukrainian-lessons-art-in-a-time-of-war-with-charlotte-higgins-and-guests\"><em>here</em></a><em>.</em></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2026/sep/01/war-of-words-my-language-lessons-in-ukraine-podcast\">Continue reading...</a>"
